<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">William IV, Landgrave of Hesse-Kassel</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1532">1532</a>–<a href="/years/1592">1592</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a> · Also known as William the Wise</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">William IV, Landgrave of Hesse-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kassel">Kassel</a>, called the Wise, was the eldest son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/philip-i-landgrave-of-hesse">Philip the Magnanimous</a>. In the division of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hesse">Hesse</a> in 1567 he received about half the land, with Kassel as his capital. He was a careful administrator and a noted astronomer whose observatory at Kassel produced one of the best <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/star-catalogue">star catalogues</a> of the age.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/william-iv-landgrave-of-hesse-kassel.jpg" alt="William IV, Landgrave of Hesse-Kassel" width="320" height="338" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Caspar van der Borcht · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Wilhelm_IV._Landgraf_von_Hessen-Kassel_Borcht.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
